WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.589
The King of Kong documentary proves that video
game scores, and mullets, are a very serious

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:12.190
business. Everyone is out to set a new speedrun
record or high score, so it's hard to keep

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:16.080
up sometimes. You can play Kickle Cubicle
until your thumbs are as thick as your neck

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.830
and never come close to the masters' scores,
but at least you'll have a good time doing

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.890
it. If getting your name etched into the annals
of gaming history is your thing, you can aim

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:29.090
really high… but there are some records
you'll have a really hard time beating.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.789
TURBO MODE KILL SCREEN IN PAC-MAN

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:37.030
Pac-Man perfection is a combination of robotic
timing, relentlessness, and adult diapers.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.510
The player's goal is to break the game by
reaching the "kill screen." That's a point

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.019
in the game's code where the screen decays
into random symbols, the result of a memory

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:49.629
shortage after level 256. Glitching Pac-Man
is the Grail of competitive retro gaming,

00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:53.850
officially reached by only seven people. There
are a few modded games and apps floating around

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:57.429
online that can start you off with the kill
screen, but it's not the same as earning it

00:00:57.429 --> 00:01:02.059
the hard way. Good luck trying it in Turbo
Mode—only two people in history ever reached

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:03.609
it that way.

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:06.049
FASTEST TIME IN SUPER MARIO BROS.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:09.479
Over the years, all kinds of players have
scrambled to beat the original Super Mario

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:13.490
Bros. on the NES in record time. Depending
on whether or not you use the Warp Zone pipes

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:17.600
to skip levels, you can have a very different
time for your overall playthrough. In terms

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.490
of clearing every level (without warping),
from start to finish, Andrew Gardikis was

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:26.789
able to beat this iconic game in just 19 minutes
and 12 seconds. On top of that, Gardikis holds

00:01:26.789 --> 00:01:30.880
the warp zone record as well, beating the
game in just 4 minutes and 57 seconds. Why

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.929
bother grabbing the mushroom when you can
just win, right?

00:01:33.929 --> 00:01:39.170
MEGA MAN X, X2, AND X3 BEATEN SIMULTANEOUSLY
WITH THE SAME CONTROLLER

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:44.130
The elite Mega Man player known online as
"agwawaf" was able to beat Mega Man X, X2,

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:50.149
and X3 with 100 percent completion in just
43 minutes and 51 seconds. While all three

00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:54.049
of those games have faster completion times,
there's a twist to this particular record:

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:59.350
agwawaf was actually playing all three games
at once with a single controller. His gamepad's

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:03.789
inputs were used across all three games simultaneously,
which allowed him to beat them all at once.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:07.509
Sure, the runs weren't perfect, and he took
damage along the way. But just think of how

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:12.560
incredible it is to beat three games at the
same time in just under 44 minutes. In fact,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.180
all three final bosses, endings, and credits
sequences all happen during his playthrough

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:20.510
at the same time. Most people can't even beat
one of these games in under an hour, let alone

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:24.250
all three at once. Just give up now, you guys.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:27.420
LONGEST MMORPG GAMEPLAY MARATHON IN WORLD
OF WARCRAFT

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.640
Hectaerina Kinumi Iglesias is no stranger
to setting unbreakable records, especially

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:36.170
when it comes to role-playing games. Going
by her online alias of Kinumi Cati, Iglesias

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:42.250
played World of Warcraft for 29 hours and
31 minutes, starting on March 29, 2014, and

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.930
finishing the next day. She set two Guinness
World Records in that time: one for the longest

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.870
video game marathon on a massively multiplayer
online role-playing game; and the other for

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:55.680
longest video game marathon on World of Warcraft.
She also holds the records for longest video

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.590
game marathon in a Japanese-style role-playing
game and longest video game marathon for any

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:04.890
Final Fantasy title, playing Final Fantasy
X for a whopping 38 hours and 6 minutes. And

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.470
that's really way too much Wakka for one sitting.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.810
THE LEGEND OF ZELDA EXTREME CHALLENGE

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:14.580
The rules of the Zelda Extreme Challenge are
harsh, like Ganon himself created it to ensure

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.420
he ultimately wins. You have to completely
skip getting the sword at the start of the

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:23.730
game—but don't worry. It gets better. You
also can't collect most treasures, you can't

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:28.720
accidentally kill overworld enemies, and you
can only use bombs and fire on bosses. Your

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.300
quest ends when you encounter the final boss,
who cannot be defeated without the treasures

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:37.160
you've skipped. While you've certainly accomplished
something, you'll still never know sweet victory.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.500
Only four people have completed the challenge
in both the first and second quest modes.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:45.050
They didn't save Hyrule, but they've more
than earned our respect.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:48.120
LONGEST GAMEPLAY MARATHON WITH A CONTROLLER
IN CALL OF DUTY

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.230
The Guinness Book of World Records marks 135
hours as the longest gameplay session of Call

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.460
of Duty, but it comes with a caveat: the record
holder was allowed to take a 10-minute break

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:02.910
for every hour of play, providing some much-needed
naptimes. While you might think that's cheating,

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:08.010
Guinness had a good reason to allow the breaks:
in a separate attempt to set a gameplay marathon

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:13.370
record, a teenager died while in his 40th
consecutive hour of Diablo 3. Indeed, spending

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:17.799
six days in a nonstop warzone would destroy
anyone's psyche. Mind you, this is the record

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:21.440
for gameplay marathons with a controller in
your hand. For a while, it was the longest

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.290
gameplay marathon ever. But you won't believe
what actually surpassed it.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.100
LONGEST GAMEPLAY MARATHON IN JUST DANCE 4

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.770
Just hearing about this California school
teacher's video game record is exhausting

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:37.390
enough. Carrie Swidecki broke the aforementioned
Call of Duty record by playing Just Dance

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:44.160
4 on Xbox 360 for 138 consecutive hours. Just
let that sink in for a moment—most people

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:50.550
feel exhausted playing Just Dance 4 for 13
minutes, let alone nearly six days. Swidecki

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.630
simultaneously set three world records while
playing a dance game that requires players

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:59.740
to move and just dance the entire time. By
dancing until the 138-hour mark, she set the

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:04.100
world records for longest video game marathon
of all time, longest marathon playing a dance

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:09.350
game, and longest marathon with a motion-sensing
game. Even more impressive? By playing Just

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:14.990
Dance 4, Swidecki dropped 80 pounds and raised
over $7,000 to support children's health-related

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.370
charities.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.080
THE WORLD'S LARGEST VIDEO GAME COLLECTION

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:23.060
Michael Thomasson might look like a regular
guy, until you realize he's arguably the most

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:28.710
dedicated hoarder and collector of video games
and consoles that ever lived. In late 2013,

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:32.690
Thomasson won the Guinness World Record for
the largest video game collection. We're talking

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:40.290
10,607 games and over 100 consoles. Thomasson
was able to sell his gargantuan set for over

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:46.670
$750,000, but he's probably going to rebuild.
How did he acquire such a library? Thomasson

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:51.150
has the connections, as he ran seven different
video game stores over the past 20 years and

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.540
has been working at several retail game stores
along the way. He even teaches college classes

00:05:55.540 --> 00:06:00.400
on retro gaming. Man, what's on the final?
Explaining what the hell Dig Dug was actually

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:00.889
about?

00:06:00.889 --> 00:06:04.840
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to see more videos like the one you

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:05.340
just saw.

